WEBVTT

00:45.086 --> 00:47.297
- Hold on.
- Sure.

00:58.433 --> 00:59.768
Doors closing.

00:59.851 --> 01:00.894
Wait!

01:01.519 --> 01:02.812
Doors opening.

01:02.896 --> 01:04.022
Thank you. Hey.

01:04.647 --> 01:06.316
- You just got home?
- Yes.

01:13.782 --> 01:14.908
What is that?

01:17.243 --> 01:18.745
It's a faucet for my sink.

01:18.828 --> 01:21.164
- It's leaking.
- I see.

01:21.247 --> 01:22.665
Your landlord could…

01:23.917 --> 01:26.586
Right. You're the landlord.

01:26.669 --> 01:29.088
Mr. Landlord.

01:29.172 --> 01:31.049
I'm still paying back the loan.

01:31.132 --> 01:33.009
But it's registered under your name.

01:33.092 --> 01:34.052
That's big.

01:35.512 --> 01:37.847
You have a decent job and a house.

01:37.931 --> 01:39.474
Lucky her.

01:40.016 --> 01:42.894
- Who?
- Your future wife.

01:49.651 --> 01:51.277
Twelfth floor.

01:52.403 --> 01:53.696
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

01:53.780 --> 01:54.781
Bye.

01:59.410 --> 02:00.995
Doors closing.

02:01.621 --> 02:02.789
Who are you?

02:04.833 --> 02:06.334
Then who are you, lady?

02:06.960 --> 02:08.336
Lady?

02:08.419 --> 02:09.838
My daughter lives here.

02:14.175 --> 02:16.052
- Hey. What?
- Hey.

02:25.979 --> 02:27.147
Hello.

02:29.732 --> 02:30.900
Hello.

02:45.498 --> 02:47.208
- Say yes.
- Say yes.

02:47.292 --> 02:50.211
- Say yes.
- Say yes.

02:51.254 --> 02:52.964
He's so cool.

02:54.257 --> 02:55.675
Why is he taking such a risk?

02:55.758 --> 02:57.677
"The end of love is marriage."

02:57.760 --> 03:00.388
Such an obvious conclusion
isn't the only answer.

03:06.728 --> 03:09.689
LEE SI-WOO

03:13.276 --> 03:14.193
I'm still at work--

03:14.277 --> 03:16.654
I think you should hurry home.

03:17.530 --> 03:18.448
What?

03:22.243 --> 03:24.454
Let me get this straight.

03:25.705 --> 03:27.916
You two are living with my daughter?

03:27.999 --> 03:29.918
- Yes. That's correct, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

03:30.418 --> 03:31.711
Until when?

03:31.794 --> 03:33.630
Until…

03:34.213 --> 03:36.466
Until we return to our homes--

03:36.549 --> 03:39.177
No, until the end of
the summer disaster prevention period.

03:39.260 --> 03:40.470
That's correct.

03:41.721 --> 03:43.806
The end of summer disaster prevention…

03:45.183 --> 03:46.643
It's still a ways off.

03:46.726 --> 03:48.269
- Correct.
- Correct.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.606
What woman in her right mind

03:51.689 --> 03:54.234
invites two men to live
with her when she lives alone?

03:54.817 --> 03:56.778
The disaster prevention period

03:56.861 --> 04:00.865
often requires spontaneous meetings, so…

04:00.949 --> 04:03.409
- Right?
- Yes. He's right.

04:04.535 --> 04:06.871
In any case,
we're sorry to have worried you.

04:08.289 --> 04:09.499
You're right.

04:09.582 --> 04:12.585
Considering my daughter's age,

04:12.669 --> 04:15.713
I am truly worried
about this living situation.

04:17.924 --> 04:19.259
What does she mean?

04:20.093 --> 04:21.844
She's past the age of getting married.

04:22.720 --> 04:24.347
By the way,

04:24.430 --> 04:27.183
was that man we met in the elevator

04:27.267 --> 04:29.143
your colleague as well?

04:29.727 --> 04:31.729
Yes, he's also on our team.

04:32.230 --> 04:33.398
- Who?
- Seok-ho.

04:33.481 --> 04:35.233
Yes. We're on the same team.

04:36.317 --> 04:37.318
Is he married?

04:37.402 --> 04:38.903
- No, not yet.
- He's single.

04:38.987 --> 04:40.989
- How old is he?
- Sorry?

04:41.072 --> 04:43.992
How old is that man?

04:44.075 --> 04:46.202
He and Director Jin
are probably the same age.

04:46.286 --> 04:48.955
- Right?
- No.

04:49.038 --> 04:51.332
He just looks very young.

04:51.416 --> 04:54.377
He's actually much older than her.

04:55.753 --> 04:57.088
He's seven years her senior.

04:57.171 --> 04:58.172
I see.

05:00.842 --> 05:04.345
Seven years? That's not a problem.

05:05.763 --> 05:06.597
Seven?

05:11.060 --> 05:13.688
Why did you come without telling me?

05:13.771 --> 05:16.482
You're unbelievable.
How could you invite strangers

05:16.566 --> 05:18.901
into your house
without discussing it with me?

05:19.485 --> 05:23.072
They're not strangers.
They're forecasters on my team.

05:24.532 --> 05:26.200
So this was why

05:26.284 --> 05:29.329
you rushed back home
when I said I was coming over.

05:29.412 --> 05:32.206
I thought you had treasure
stashed somewhere.

05:32.874 --> 05:34.167
Good grief.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.544
It's work-related.

05:36.627 --> 05:38.338
It's the disaster prevention period,

05:38.421 --> 05:39.881
and I'm still a rookie director.

05:39.964 --> 05:42.050
I needed their help, so I invited them.

05:42.133 --> 05:43.217
Goodness.

05:43.718 --> 05:46.554
You're not the type
to ask others for help.

05:46.637 --> 05:49.098
You don't even ask for help
when you're very sick.

05:50.808 --> 05:52.727
That's enough. Let's talk outside.

05:52.810 --> 05:54.479
- Hurry.
- Talk here. It's hot out.

05:54.562 --> 05:56.564
- Come with me.
- Hey.

05:57.774 --> 05:58.816
But I--

05:58.900 --> 06:00.693
- Good…
- Goodbye, ma'am.

06:24.133 --> 06:26.385
MOM

06:34.018 --> 06:35.269
Hey, Mom.

06:36.354 --> 06:37.855
I know.

06:37.939 --> 06:41.150
Something urgent came up,
so I couldn't make it.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.487
I'm sorry for not making it
to your birthday.

06:45.655 --> 06:47.156
What? What handbag?

06:52.411 --> 06:54.330
- Did you go shopping again?
- That's not--

06:54.413 --> 06:55.957
You're so carefree.

06:56.040 --> 06:59.961
Are you saying that
I'm spending thoughtlessly?

07:01.045 --> 07:02.130
If you aren't,

07:02.839 --> 07:05.299
you wouldn't have bought
something that expensive.

07:09.178 --> 07:10.388
Oh, that.

07:11.222 --> 07:12.932
I see.

07:13.766 --> 07:16.394
No, Yu-jin was the one who picked it.

07:17.019 --> 07:18.646
I told you.

07:18.729 --> 07:20.982
She has good taste
and she's a good person.

07:21.065 --> 07:24.235
But you always nitpick
and compare her to Ha-kyung.

07:24.318 --> 07:26.446
My Yu-jin has a lot of strengths.

07:30.700 --> 07:32.660
Okay.

07:32.743 --> 07:35.329
Call her some time
and treat her to a meal.

07:36.038 --> 07:37.165
Okay.

07:38.541 --> 07:39.709
Bye.

07:44.422 --> 07:48.217
Damn it. Are you an idiot?

07:50.428 --> 07:52.847
- Lee Dong-gook shoots!
- Rebound!

07:52.930 --> 07:55.183
They box each other out!

07:55.266 --> 07:56.767
Will he pass or shoot?

07:58.060 --> 08:01.147
He sinks the three-pointer!
Here comes Yang Hui-seung.

08:01.230 --> 08:03.691
He misses. And misses again.

08:04.942 --> 08:06.277
Ahn Jung-hwan!

08:06.360 --> 08:09.071
Yoon Gyeong-sin with the rebound.
They go on a fast break!

08:09.155 --> 08:09.989
Hey!

08:12.617 --> 08:15.620
Ahn Jung-hwan scores!

08:16.496 --> 08:17.747
That's good.

08:18.706 --> 08:19.540
Good.

08:23.044 --> 08:25.421
Hey…

08:27.089 --> 08:30.468
You should have told me.

08:33.221 --> 08:34.472
About the handbag.

08:36.807 --> 08:40.770
Her friends loved it
when she carried it with her today.

08:40.853 --> 08:43.272
She called me and said she was so happy.

08:43.856 --> 08:46.692
They commented on how she had
such a wonderful daughter-in-law.

08:48.361 --> 08:50.112
I'm sorry for what I said

08:50.947 --> 08:51.864
that day.

08:54.158 --> 08:55.243
It's fine.

08:57.411 --> 08:58.538
By the way,

08:59.580 --> 09:01.249
where did you get the money?

09:01.874 --> 09:04.877
I'm sure it exceeded
the maximum limit of our credit card.

09:04.961 --> 09:07.964
I used my summer bonus
and some money I had on the side.

09:09.882 --> 09:14.178
I knew we'd be too busy
to go on a summer vacation.

09:15.429 --> 09:18.182
So I decided
to just spend it on your mother.

09:21.018 --> 09:22.395
Thank you, Yu-jin.

09:23.688 --> 09:26.440
I was being extremely inconsiderate.

09:28.192 --> 09:29.360
Whatever.

09:29.443 --> 09:31.946
Can you please forgive me this once?

09:38.035 --> 09:40.246
I'm so sorry. I was wrong.

09:41.372 --> 09:42.665
Do you want a massage?

09:45.334 --> 09:47.211
I'm really sorry. I'll treat you better.

09:49.130 --> 09:52.967
I bet the bills are much higher
now that you live with two other people.

09:53.050 --> 09:54.760
Are they paying their share?

09:54.844 --> 09:56.262
I invited them to live with me.

09:58.222 --> 10:01.100
Make sure they pay
their share for all the bills.

10:01.684 --> 10:03.227
Mom, I'm their director.

10:03.311 --> 10:04.854
Goodness.

10:06.814 --> 10:08.357
I know you're a halfwit.

10:12.194 --> 10:14.530
Director Jin's mother
must have taken a liking

10:15.990 --> 10:18.909
to Assistant Director Shin.

10:18.993 --> 10:21.203
Still, Director Jin's opinions matter too.

10:21.287 --> 10:23.998
She shouldn't be so forceful.

10:24.915 --> 10:28.544
Seok-ho tends
to give off an indifferent vibe.

10:28.628 --> 10:32.548
He may not be perfect

10:32.632 --> 10:34.675
and seem unfriendly,

10:36.052 --> 10:38.846
but he'd be a decent husband.
Don't you think so?

10:41.641 --> 10:45.019
I'm telling you.
They don't suit each other.

10:46.020 --> 10:48.397
Seok-ho and Director Jin

10:48.898 --> 10:50.983
have absolutely nothing in common.

10:51.567 --> 10:53.361
They have different hobbies and tastes.

10:53.444 --> 10:55.071
They just can't get along.

10:55.154 --> 10:56.822
Come on.

10:58.658 --> 11:01.452
You never know.

11:01.535 --> 11:05.456
At times, even the most impossible
becomes possible.

11:05.539 --> 11:07.625
Especially when it comes to men and women.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.168
Gosh.

11:09.669 --> 11:13.297
You never know. You're so naive.

11:35.736 --> 11:36.821
By the way,

11:37.405 --> 11:40.950
I heard there's another colleague
who lives above you.

11:41.575 --> 11:43.994
- Who? Assistant Director Shin?
- That's his position?

11:45.287 --> 11:48.999
He was dressed so neatly.
He seemed like a nice guy.

11:49.083 --> 11:50.709
- Right?
- Mind your own business.

11:50.793 --> 11:52.503
- The cab is here.
- Come on.

11:52.586 --> 11:55.047
It's only natural for me to be interested.

11:55.131 --> 11:57.466
Don't be so cold to him.

11:57.550 --> 11:59.468
Take your time and get to know him.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.720
Who knows what'll happen, right?

12:01.804 --> 12:03.722
You can go, sir. Get home safe, Mom.

12:08.018 --> 12:09.979
Assistant Director Shin?

12:11.605 --> 12:13.607
A seven-year age gap is nothing.

12:33.002 --> 12:34.920
Did your mother go home?

12:36.589 --> 12:37.631
Yes.

12:40.759 --> 12:42.094
Si-woo…

12:42.803 --> 12:43.888
doesn't believe in marriage.

12:46.223 --> 12:49.977
He doesn't want to marry anyone.

12:53.606 --> 12:57.735
Ha-kyung doesn't sincerely date anyone
if they're not a marriage prospect.

13:00.196 --> 13:01.989
You knew that, right?

13:08.412 --> 13:10.372
- How about a beer?
- Do you want a beer?

13:14.418 --> 13:15.961
- Let's have a drink.
- Okay.

13:28.849 --> 13:30.935
I met with Reporter Chae.

13:32.728 --> 13:34.897
She said you're not interested
in getting married.

13:37.024 --> 13:37.858
Right.

13:44.782 --> 13:46.534
Can I ask why?

13:47.368 --> 13:49.328
I don't think marriage suits me.

13:50.037 --> 13:53.374
And I wonder if marriage has to be
the next step when in love.

13:56.085 --> 13:58.587
Being tied to each other as a family

13:58.671 --> 14:00.130
makes me uncomfortable.

14:01.298 --> 14:04.468
And I don't want the person I love

14:05.886 --> 14:07.263
to carry my burdens either.

14:13.936 --> 14:17.273
So for you, having a family is a burden.

14:17.856 --> 14:19.149
You know why.

14:22.486 --> 14:26.156
That's why I decided
that I would never get married.

14:32.329 --> 14:33.372
Are you disappointed?

14:34.081 --> 14:35.249
No.

14:36.584 --> 14:38.043
It's just…

14:38.127 --> 14:40.671
I've never thought about a relationship

14:40.754 --> 14:43.048
that didn't lead to marriage.

14:44.466 --> 14:45.718
But you see,

14:45.801 --> 14:48.220
that doesn't mean
I'm not sincere toward you.

14:48.846 --> 14:51.807
I don't consider what we have a fling.

14:51.891 --> 14:54.184
- My feelings are very genuine.
- I know.

14:58.564 --> 14:59.607
I'm just curious.

15:01.442 --> 15:04.904
What could be
at the end of our relationship?

15:07.531 --> 15:09.450
If it's not marriage,

15:10.409 --> 15:13.913
what could be awaiting us at the end?

15:18.375 --> 15:21.170
Sleep is heavily affected by temperature.

15:22.046 --> 15:23.088
High temperature

15:23.881 --> 15:26.133
stimulates our central nervous system

15:26.759 --> 15:28.552
and hinders deep sleep.

15:43.317 --> 15:46.236
On such nights, we become lost in thought.

15:48.113 --> 15:49.615
When that happens,

15:50.115 --> 15:52.201
we end up having complicated feelings

15:52.284 --> 15:55.329
and that leads to more thoughts.

15:56.413 --> 15:59.333
And eventually, we become
even more lost in thought.

16:02.795 --> 16:03.921
It's hot.

16:04.004 --> 16:06.548
Gosh, it's hot.

16:07.424 --> 16:12.805
EPISODE 10
TROPICAL NIGHT

16:13.389 --> 16:17.309
Last night, the lowest temperature
in Seoul was 25°C.

16:17.393 --> 16:20.479
It was our first tropical night this year.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.481
The weather is hot this morning as well.

16:22.564 --> 16:26.402
- Many areas will be 31°C or higher today.
- Good morning.

16:27.027 --> 16:30.280
- It'll be sweltering hot today too.
- I can't take it.

16:30.364 --> 16:33.450
The monsoon rain
should have cooled down the heat.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.035
Tonight will be hot as well.

16:35.119 --> 16:36.996
It's very humid too.

16:37.079 --> 16:39.665
- Sensible temperature will be even higher.
- Take care of yourselves.

16:39.748 --> 16:42.501
- That concludes the weather forecast.
- Are you that worried?

16:43.252 --> 16:45.921
It looks like you didn't
sleep much last night.

16:46.005 --> 16:47.423
It was pretty hot.

16:50.843 --> 16:52.511
We're an inconvenience, aren't we?

16:52.594 --> 16:54.096
You can't even open your door freely.

16:54.847 --> 16:55.931
Thankfully,

16:56.015 --> 16:58.726
I don't sleep with the door open
no matter how hot it gets.

16:58.809 --> 17:00.185
Don't worry about me.

17:01.937 --> 17:03.063
Anyway, I'm sorry.

17:03.731 --> 17:06.650
I'll go back home as soon as possible.

17:06.734 --> 17:08.444
You don't have to rush.

17:15.284 --> 17:17.786
Goodness. Look at him.

17:17.870 --> 17:19.747
He must have not gotten any sleep either.

17:20.330 --> 17:21.165
What?

17:21.749 --> 17:24.043
The tropical nights
will worsen for the time being.

17:24.126 --> 17:26.211
You're going to have a bumpy ride.

17:26.920 --> 17:28.964
I'm going to get ready first.

17:29.048 --> 17:30.090
Okay.

17:39.725 --> 17:41.185
Did you not sleep well?

17:41.268 --> 17:42.728
It was pretty hot.

17:45.272 --> 17:46.273
It was.

17:52.237 --> 17:53.489
Let's see.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.784
You've all been waiting for this.

17:56.867 --> 17:59.745
We brought the top three items
for newlyweds.

17:59.828 --> 18:03.123
It's really hot these days.
An AC, a fridge, and a washing machine.

18:03.207 --> 18:06.251
- This set is only available on our--
- I wonder what's on the news.

18:06.335 --> 18:11.215
Statistics Korea has analyzed
the marriage rate and birth rate to--

18:12.007 --> 18:14.134
- Do you want some coffee?
- I'll make toast.

18:14.218 --> 18:15.344
- Good.
- Okay.

18:20.099 --> 18:21.683
Doors opening.

18:29.566 --> 18:32.528
You never know.

18:32.611 --> 18:36.573
At times, even the most impossible
becomes possible.

18:36.657 --> 18:38.742
Especially when it comes to men and women.

18:39.284 --> 18:40.410
Gosh.

18:40.494 --> 18:42.538
You never know.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.166
- Hey, did you have breakfast?
- Hey.

18:51.713 --> 18:53.757
Doors closing.

18:57.261 --> 18:59.721
It's too hot to make kimchi.

18:59.805 --> 19:02.516
Mom, why are you buying
so many young radishes?

19:02.599 --> 19:05.519
Don't you know how tasty it is
if you make kimchi with this

19:05.602 --> 19:06.979
and have it with cold noodles?

19:07.062 --> 19:09.481
So exactly why
are you making so much of it?

19:09.565 --> 19:11.233
I have my reasons.

19:11.316 --> 19:13.610
- Here.
- Okay. Thank you.

19:13.694 --> 19:14.903
Hey, we need to hurry.

19:14.987 --> 19:17.906
We're short on time
if we want to make this all today.

19:19.533 --> 19:20.409
What reasons?

19:20.993 --> 19:22.619
You terrify me

19:22.703 --> 19:25.455
whenever you say that.
What's up your sleeve?

19:27.374 --> 19:28.709
You see…

19:29.877 --> 19:33.130
It's about the guy
who lives above Ha-kyung.

19:33.213 --> 19:34.506
What?

19:35.132 --> 19:36.383
You know,

19:36.466 --> 19:40.888
- the one who kept those side dishes.
- Apartment number 1302?

19:40.971 --> 19:44.308
He works with Ha-kyung on her team.

19:44.391 --> 19:45.559
Really?

19:46.143 --> 19:47.686
Then why didn't he say anything?

19:47.769 --> 19:48.854
What?

19:49.438 --> 19:51.565
- Do you know him well?
- Of course not.

19:51.648 --> 19:54.151
We just ran into each other
a couple of times.

19:54.651 --> 19:56.528
He seemed like a decent guy.

19:57.112 --> 20:00.073
There you go,
trying to hook Ha-kyung up again.

20:00.157 --> 20:03.911
How about you help me out
and look into him for me?

20:04.536 --> 20:06.997
- Look into what?
- What else?

20:07.080 --> 20:12.586
Find out if he's
a good match with Ha-kyung.

20:13.295 --> 20:14.379
Okay?

20:19.384 --> 20:21.929
Seoul's aerological observation data is…

20:24.806 --> 20:28.101
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

20:34.608 --> 20:35.859
Assistant Director Oh.

20:36.902 --> 20:38.695
- Assistant Director Oh!
- What?

20:39.279 --> 20:40.447
What? What is it?

20:40.948 --> 20:43.992
It's about Taebaek's AWS levels.

20:44.076 --> 20:45.619
Is this right?

20:45.702 --> 20:47.579
Yes, it is.

20:47.663 --> 20:48.956
What's wrong?

20:51.208 --> 20:52.834
Did you not sleep well last night?

20:52.918 --> 20:55.254
It was way too hot.

20:56.213 --> 20:59.049
Our youngest kid was tossing and turning,

20:59.132 --> 21:00.801
so I couldn't sleep either.

21:00.884 --> 21:02.636
I'm so out of it today.

21:02.719 --> 21:04.721
We can't leave the AC on all night long.

21:05.889 --> 21:07.015
And your husband?

21:07.099 --> 21:09.643
Well, he's busy studying.

21:10.310 --> 21:12.187
Since he wanted to try it out,

21:12.271 --> 21:14.273
I told him to just go to town.

21:15.899 --> 21:17.693
This won't do.

21:17.776 --> 21:19.903
I'll go splash some cold water on my face.

21:21.154 --> 21:22.239
Gosh.

21:26.034 --> 21:28.662
It'd be quicker if she took
the Grade Five exam instead.

21:30.789 --> 21:32.582
She had the best grade

21:32.666 --> 21:34.501
among Grade Seven test-takers
when she came here.

21:34.584 --> 21:37.879
She was clever, quick,
and had great leadership skills.

21:38.547 --> 21:41.508
Everyone thought
she'd become the next director.

21:42.009 --> 21:44.177
But then came housework and raising kids.

21:44.261 --> 21:45.637
She overworked herself.

21:45.721 --> 21:48.140
Now, she's stuck in her position.

21:48.223 --> 21:51.685
Plus, her husband quit
to prepare for the state exam.

21:51.768 --> 21:53.145
She has a lot on her plate.

21:53.729 --> 21:56.064
I'm impressed
that she's still going strong.

21:56.148 --> 21:57.107
Don't you think so?

21:57.691 --> 22:00.027
She has no choice. She's the breadwinner.

22:00.110 --> 22:02.404
Right. You're right.

22:04.031 --> 22:06.408
Did you not sleep well either?

22:07.034 --> 22:09.077
Yes. The tropical nights.

22:09.161 --> 22:10.245
Let's get back to work.

22:13.206 --> 22:15.917
Even those who analyze
the weather can't beat the heat.

22:20.589 --> 22:21.757
Hey, Yu-jin.

22:22.341 --> 22:24.301
What? Wait.

22:24.843 --> 22:26.470
What's a senior writer doing here?

22:26.553 --> 22:30.265
There's nothing interesting
to report nowadays.

22:31.308 --> 22:33.018
That's why you're here?

22:33.101 --> 22:34.811
You know what they say.

22:34.895 --> 22:37.439
"When in need of a scoop, go to the KMA."

22:37.522 --> 22:39.983
I'm sure I'll get something
if I stay here long enough.

22:41.109 --> 22:42.486
By the way,

22:42.569 --> 22:43.945
how's the cafeteria food here?

22:44.696 --> 22:45.572
It's not bad.

22:45.655 --> 22:47.199
Okay. See you around.

22:56.249 --> 22:57.292
Hello?

22:57.375 --> 22:59.169
I heard Heo Ju-yeong is there.

23:03.215 --> 23:05.967
- How did you know?
- Damn it. That's not important.

23:06.051 --> 23:08.595
Don't think about coming back
if he steals your scoop.

23:09.721 --> 23:11.890
There's no scoop to begin with.

23:11.973 --> 23:14.768
You don't know
what that leech is capable of.

23:14.851 --> 23:17.187
During his time there,

23:17.270 --> 23:19.481
he will find something to write about.

23:19.564 --> 23:20.690
Keep an eye on him.

23:21.399 --> 23:23.193
Everyone knows that's your home ground.

23:23.276 --> 23:26.113
You'll lose face if he steals your scoop.

23:27.030 --> 23:29.241
- Okay.
- Think of your hardworking colleagues.

23:29.324 --> 23:31.952
- It's all on you.
- I get it.

23:35.872 --> 23:38.375
Hello, I'm from Munmin Daily.

23:42.087 --> 23:45.757
As of now, we cannot locate
the stationary front.

23:45.841 --> 23:48.343
Due to the expansion
of the North Pacific's anticyclone,

23:48.426 --> 23:51.304
our peninsula is suffering
from high temperature and humidity.

23:51.388 --> 23:53.473
The heatwave will continue at this rate,

23:53.557 --> 23:57.644
and the tropical nights
will be 25°C or higher.

23:59.563 --> 24:01.106
If the tropical nights continue,

24:01.189 --> 24:03.108
people will use more electricity.

24:03.191 --> 24:05.944
Then a blackout could occur.

24:06.820 --> 24:09.030
That's true,
but the media is also a problem.

24:09.114 --> 24:11.158
Using strong words

24:11.241 --> 24:12.909
such as "steaming hot",

24:12.993 --> 24:14.953
"the hottest", and "deadly heat"

24:15.036 --> 24:16.705
will only provoke people.

24:16.788 --> 24:18.039
Goodness.

24:19.833 --> 24:23.920
We've sent out materials
explaining the heat waves to the media.

24:24.004 --> 24:26.756
We will do our best
in dealing with the media.

24:28.800 --> 24:29.676
Okay.

24:29.759 --> 24:31.553
- Hurry up.
- What?

24:34.723 --> 24:36.558
- Next time.
- Okay.

24:38.310 --> 24:40.395
What is it? Is there a problem?

24:40.478 --> 24:41.438
Not at all.

24:51.740 --> 24:53.658
That will be all
for the forecast discussion.

24:53.742 --> 24:55.243
Good work, guys.

24:55.327 --> 24:57.704
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

25:07.339 --> 25:08.798
We need to talk.

25:18.058 --> 25:19.184
What's going on?

25:20.268 --> 25:21.478
Let's sit down.

25:43.333 --> 25:46.294
Never in my wildest dreams
did I think I'd ask you this.

25:47.337 --> 25:49.631
But how's married life?

25:53.593 --> 25:54.594
Are you talking to me?

25:54.678 --> 25:57.180
- Were you asking me?
- Be serious.

25:57.764 --> 25:59.599
I'm genuinely curious.

26:00.642 --> 26:01.685
What is it?

26:02.310 --> 26:03.728
Did Si-woo propose to you?

26:05.105 --> 26:06.356
Forget that I asked.

26:06.439 --> 26:08.733
Fine. I'll be serious.

26:10.735 --> 26:13.571
Let's see. How is married life?

26:14.572 --> 26:15.949
It's not easy

26:16.032 --> 26:19.327
to define it as good,
bad, or anything else.

26:19.911 --> 26:21.579
It's hard to explain.

26:22.998 --> 26:24.165
Is that so?

26:25.041 --> 26:29.754
I thought everything would be peachy
if we just loved each other.

26:29.838 --> 26:31.631
But it turned out I was wrong.

26:31.715 --> 26:35.927
There's so much
we need to look out for and take care of.

26:36.011 --> 26:38.722
I thought it'd just double
since there were two of us.

26:38.805 --> 26:41.182
But rather, it increased tenfold.

26:42.684 --> 26:43.685
Well…

26:43.768 --> 26:47.981
As you know,
it wasn't easy for us to get married.

26:48.732 --> 26:52.402
I think I feel pressured
to maintain a happy married life.

26:52.902 --> 26:55.947
I become quite irritable
with the smallest things.

26:59.034 --> 27:00.785
And…

27:02.245 --> 27:05.582
And in the past,
I wasn't too concerned about others.

27:06.333 --> 27:07.834
But once we got married,

27:07.917 --> 27:12.922
I became aware of those
around us whom I didn't think much of.

27:13.673 --> 27:16.301
And on the other hand,
those with whom I used to be close

27:16.384 --> 27:18.595
make me feel uncomfortable now.

27:20.472 --> 27:23.224
Anyway, you see each other's flaws better

27:23.308 --> 27:25.852
when you start living together.

27:26.436 --> 27:29.856
Understanding and accepting them
aren't easy either.

27:45.205 --> 27:47.749
Isn't that nuisance from Munmin Daily?

27:47.832 --> 27:48.917
What?

27:53.671 --> 27:55.215
What's with you guys these days?

27:56.091 --> 27:57.884
I get that you're in need of a scoop,

27:57.967 --> 27:59.886
but that's just not right.

28:04.891 --> 28:06.226
One minute.

28:10.647 --> 28:12.315
Can we talk?

28:17.195 --> 28:19.656
Here's your strawberry smoothie.

28:20.657 --> 28:22.158
I'm busy.

28:23.076 --> 28:25.245
I just wanted to treat you to something.

28:25.328 --> 28:28.289
Then you could have just
bought me some drinks.

28:32.085 --> 28:34.504
You've become prettier
after getting married.

28:34.587 --> 28:35.880
Is that so?

28:35.964 --> 28:38.758
I heard your husband works here.

28:39.426 --> 28:40.593
He does.

28:43.805 --> 28:46.057
Do you have any juicy information?

28:46.141 --> 28:48.601
Rumors are fine too.

28:48.685 --> 28:53.148
Or perhaps,
an intense rivalry among the teams.

28:53.231 --> 28:57.110
Even bullying or
sexual harassment cases would work

28:57.193 --> 28:58.987
since they're civil servants.

29:00.989 --> 29:02.198
Speaking of which…

29:02.907 --> 29:04.117
What is it?

29:04.200 --> 29:08.329
Recently, I heard that
the higher-ups were having a power grab.

29:09.414 --> 29:10.874
Hold on. Who are?

29:10.957 --> 29:12.959
What kind of a power grab?

29:13.543 --> 29:15.295
Wait. By higher-ups…

29:16.171 --> 29:17.922
The Vice Administrator and Administrator?

29:18.006 --> 29:19.674
Higher. Even higher.

29:19.758 --> 29:21.134
Even higher than them.

29:22.177 --> 29:24.679
The mT and mP.

29:25.764 --> 29:26.973
The mT…

29:27.640 --> 29:29.017
and mP?

29:35.732 --> 29:37.025
- Gosh.
- What are you doing?

29:38.485 --> 29:39.569
That's Yu-jin.

29:40.069 --> 29:41.571
Isn't that Reporter Heo Ju-yeong

29:41.654 --> 29:43.072
from Munmin Daily?

29:43.740 --> 29:45.033
I don't know.

29:45.116 --> 29:46.910
His nickname is Butcher Heo.

29:46.993 --> 29:48.036
Is that so?

29:48.620 --> 29:51.122
If he puts his mind to it,

29:51.206 --> 29:53.583
he could get anyone fired.

29:53.666 --> 29:56.002
But why is a society journalist here?

29:56.085 --> 29:58.213
And why is Reporter Chae with him?

30:09.641 --> 30:10.975
What's mT?

30:11.768 --> 30:13.394
What is that?

30:14.395 --> 30:16.523
Is it short for someone's name? Who is it?

30:18.775 --> 30:20.109
Well, mT stands for

30:21.444 --> 30:22.904
"Maritime Tropical air mass."

30:22.987 --> 30:24.948
And mP stands
for "Maritime Polar air mass."

30:26.199 --> 30:30.036
During summertime,
these two air masses have a power grab.

30:32.288 --> 30:35.124
You can't get a scoop here
when you don't even know the basics.

30:40.004 --> 30:41.798
Will you really stay here?

30:45.510 --> 30:46.719
Simply put,

30:47.262 --> 30:51.057
you want me to leave your turf, right?

30:51.641 --> 30:53.101
I'm just saying that

30:53.184 --> 30:55.937
it'll be hard for me to do my job

30:56.020 --> 31:00.108
if someone as great as you
steals such trivial scoops.

31:01.317 --> 31:03.319
What if I refuse to leave?

31:03.403 --> 31:07.156
Then I'll write up an article
that would cause a stir in society.

31:07.824 --> 31:10.493
I'd rather be an idiot
who can't think straight

31:11.077 --> 31:13.955
than an incompetent person
who can't even do her job right.

31:14.539 --> 31:16.165
You've gotten good at this.

31:16.833 --> 31:18.877
I'll take that as a compliment, sir.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.603
I can't believe he's my senior.

31:37.270 --> 31:38.897
What kind of a journalist is--

31:41.274 --> 31:42.525
Are you okay?

31:43.318 --> 31:44.360
I'm fine.

31:48.114 --> 31:48.990
Wait.

31:51.075 --> 31:52.869
Can we talk for a minute?

31:58.291 --> 32:00.168
Time sure flies.

32:00.251 --> 32:02.837
I still remember
my first day here in my winter jacket.

32:03.504 --> 32:04.672
Really?

32:05.673 --> 32:09.052
It feels like it's been ages
since I got married.

32:13.056 --> 32:14.223
Why did you want to talk?

32:21.230 --> 32:22.899
How did you feel

32:23.858 --> 32:26.361
when I told you that I wasn't interested

32:27.111 --> 32:28.655
in getting married?

32:37.497 --> 32:38.790
Simply put,

32:40.041 --> 32:41.000
I was speechless.

32:42.752 --> 32:44.045
"What's his deal?"

32:44.128 --> 32:45.964
"Then why is he dating me?"

32:47.215 --> 32:49.842
All sorts of thoughts
went through my head.

32:51.386 --> 32:52.387
And then?

32:54.722 --> 32:57.225
I knew that we weren't dating

32:57.308 --> 32:59.477
with marriage in mind.

32:59.560 --> 33:01.437
But in the end,

33:01.521 --> 33:04.148
we were looking
at different paths in life.

33:06.275 --> 33:10.196
I realized that
we didn't share the same future.

33:19.497 --> 33:21.040
I think that's when it all began.

33:23.626 --> 33:26.295
I thought,
"We're going to break up one day."

33:28.047 --> 33:30.425
Then I slowly began falling out of love.

33:33.678 --> 33:35.638
And that's when I met Ki-jun.

34:02.123 --> 34:03.624
I think that's when it all began.

34:04.208 --> 34:06.836
I thought,
"We're going to break up one day."

34:08.212 --> 34:10.715
Then I slowly began falling out of love.

34:24.020 --> 34:26.189
What?

34:26.272 --> 34:28.149
What's with Yeouido's current temperature?

34:32.111 --> 34:33.529
Is something wrong?

34:33.613 --> 34:35.448
It's 36.7°C.

34:36.032 --> 34:39.160
That's seven degrees higher
than neighboring areas.

34:39.243 --> 34:40.953
Did you do proper MQC?

34:42.163 --> 34:43.831
Well, I did look at it but…

34:45.291 --> 34:47.168
You looked at it, but what?

34:47.794 --> 34:49.253
Wait. One minute, sir.

34:49.962 --> 34:52.590
Remove the information
from the prevention portal site.

34:52.673 --> 34:55.927
- Do it before it causes more confusion.
- Yes, ma'am. One second.

34:56.010 --> 34:58.596
- Hold on. This is…
- I'll do it.

35:16.114 --> 35:18.032
What? What's wrong with this?

35:26.165 --> 35:27.708
Is something wrong?

35:28.960 --> 35:31.796
Something's wrong
with Yeouido's temperature.

35:32.296 --> 35:33.714
I think it's just an error.

35:34.298 --> 35:35.341
An error?

35:39.512 --> 35:40.555
Let me see.

35:50.022 --> 35:51.023
Seok-ho.

35:53.401 --> 35:54.360
So…

35:55.027 --> 35:56.988
what will happen to Assistant Director Oh?

35:57.488 --> 36:00.867
Her MQC mistake on
the AWS is considered neglect of duty.

36:00.950 --> 36:03.661
They'll go by the rules
and she'll be warned or disciplined.

36:03.744 --> 36:06.539
That's too harsh. It was just a mistake.

36:10.918 --> 36:14.088
- You tend to be really naive at times.
- What?

36:14.172 --> 36:15.840
We're civil servants.

36:15.923 --> 36:17.884
We're not allowed to make mistakes.

36:26.767 --> 36:28.060
Where are you going?

36:29.145 --> 36:30.438
To the toilet.

36:35.026 --> 36:36.194
What should we do?

36:36.277 --> 36:38.779
You need to report this
to the Director General, right?

36:38.863 --> 36:40.573
How long was the error up for?

36:40.656 --> 36:42.074
Probably less than five minutes.

36:44.785 --> 36:47.830
I'll take care of it.
You can get back to work.

36:47.914 --> 36:48.873
Yes, ma'am.

37:05.014 --> 37:06.098
Thank you.

37:10.770 --> 37:13.397
I don't usually make
such trivial mistakes.

37:13.481 --> 37:14.482
I know.

37:14.565 --> 37:16.150
This was a first.

37:16.234 --> 37:17.401
I'm sorry.

37:18.236 --> 37:21.030
I haven't been getting any sleep lately.

37:21.614 --> 37:24.700
Goodness, I know I shouldn't make excuses.

37:26.244 --> 37:27.286
I'm sorry.

37:29.538 --> 37:32.500
Why don't you go to the night-duty room
and nap for an hour?

37:33.376 --> 37:36.254
- Don't I need to report this?
- I'll take care of it.

37:37.505 --> 37:38.547
Thank you.

37:43.427 --> 37:45.638
Look, Director Jin.

37:47.306 --> 37:50.101
You shouldn't get married.

37:52.520 --> 37:55.481
You may be offended to hear this.

37:56.274 --> 37:58.776
But when I heard
that you had called off your marriage,

37:59.360 --> 38:01.070
I actually envied you.

38:03.406 --> 38:05.616
Only those who are lucky can do that.

38:05.700 --> 38:09.287
Those of us who got married and had kids

38:09.370 --> 38:11.247
because we thought we were obliged to…

38:13.416 --> 38:15.084
There's not much we can do.

38:17.753 --> 38:20.965
You should enjoy
a carefree and comfortable life.

38:22.550 --> 38:24.385
Doing whatever you want

38:25.678 --> 38:28.347
and enjoying all the free time you have.

38:34.645 --> 38:36.355
- That's you.
- Don't be absurd.

38:36.439 --> 38:37.606
What?

38:37.690 --> 38:40.192
- Are we late?
- Students, please follow me.

38:40.276 --> 38:41.485
- Okay.
- Okay.

38:48.034 --> 38:49.076
Hello?

38:49.160 --> 38:51.370
Did Bo-mi not go to school today?

38:54.707 --> 38:56.459
She's on a field trip.

38:57.126 --> 38:58.461
Why do you ask?

38:58.544 --> 38:59.920
She's here.

39:00.504 --> 39:02.340
- "Here"?
- The KMA.

39:02.423 --> 39:04.050
Anyway, I'll call you back.

39:08.846 --> 39:10.139
Why would she…

39:19.482 --> 39:21.984
You should have called me
when you arrived here.

39:22.068 --> 39:23.402
Then I would have given you

39:23.486 --> 39:26.030
and your friends
a complete tour of this place.

39:26.113 --> 39:27.573
But you're a civil servant.

39:28.240 --> 39:30.326
You shouldn't abuse
your authority like that.

39:31.994 --> 39:34.080
Right. You're right.

39:35.039 --> 39:37.124
So where did you visit?

39:37.208 --> 39:38.959
The Forecast and
Earthquake and Volcano Bureaus.

39:39.043 --> 39:40.127
I see.

39:40.711 --> 39:41.879
How does it feel to see us?

39:41.962 --> 39:45.174
Don't you think we work hard?

39:46.717 --> 39:48.052
I already knew that.

39:48.135 --> 39:49.095
What?

39:49.178 --> 39:50.679
Mom once said

39:51.972 --> 39:53.641
only those who are smart

39:53.724 --> 39:55.267
appreciate the KMA's hard work.

39:56.644 --> 39:57.853
That's right.

39:57.937 --> 39:59.980
Of course. Since you know that as well,

40:00.064 --> 40:02.108
that makes you smart too.

40:06.570 --> 40:08.489
Are you coming tomorrow too?

40:08.572 --> 40:11.242
No, next week. Why?

40:12.493 --> 40:15.246
You see, the cafeteria here
has really tasty food.

40:15.329 --> 40:16.664
I'll buy you a meal.

40:16.747 --> 40:18.165
Okay? So call me.

40:18.249 --> 40:21.252
I can abuse that much authority, right?

40:22.628 --> 40:24.880
Well, I'll think about it.

40:25.798 --> 40:26.757
Okay.

40:27.425 --> 40:30.511
Give it some thought. In a good light.

40:36.267 --> 40:38.102
Why did you go there out of the blue?

40:38.185 --> 40:40.271
I told you. It was a field trip.

40:40.354 --> 40:42.356
But why the KMA of all places?

40:42.440 --> 40:45.192
The teacher said
I needed to leave a record of visiting

40:45.276 --> 40:47.528
a science-related place
if I wanted to go to my dream school.

40:47.611 --> 40:48.779
That's why.

40:48.863 --> 40:50.906
Then you could have told me beforehand.

40:50.990 --> 40:53.075
You would have dissuaded me from going.

40:53.159 --> 40:53.993
What?

40:54.076 --> 40:55.619
You're always like that.

40:55.703 --> 40:57.663
You don't call Dad
even when it's important

40:57.746 --> 40:58.956
since you don't want to bother him.

40:59.039 --> 41:00.875
You keep everything bottled up.

41:00.958 --> 41:02.668
I deserve to know.

41:04.670 --> 41:06.422
What do you need to know?

41:06.505 --> 41:08.382
Exactly how important his job is.

41:08.466 --> 41:10.176
How important was it

41:10.259 --> 41:13.137
that he neglected us
and devoted his life to it?

41:14.263 --> 41:15.764
Don't I deserve to know?

41:19.435 --> 41:20.769
So what did you find out?

41:20.853 --> 41:22.104
I've only been there once.

41:22.188 --> 41:23.522
So you'll go again?

41:23.606 --> 41:25.065
Once more next week.

41:38.829 --> 41:40.498
Did something good happen?

41:41.540 --> 41:42.583
You know what?

41:42.666 --> 41:46.837
My daughter came
to the KMA on a field trip.

41:49.548 --> 41:51.759
Do you know what's really fascinating?

41:52.468 --> 41:53.719
My daughter…

41:54.637 --> 41:56.222
takes after me.

41:58.140 --> 42:00.643
But isn't that a given?

42:00.726 --> 42:01.852
It is.

42:03.103 --> 42:06.732
Your children always amaze you.

42:07.608 --> 42:09.610
Dealing with my daughter is
the hardest thing.

42:10.194 --> 42:12.321
But then again, she's the one

42:12.404 --> 42:14.740
who makes me smile the most.

42:15.866 --> 42:17.743
- Gosh.
- Do you love her that much?

42:18.661 --> 42:20.829
Get married and have a baby yourself.

42:20.913 --> 42:22.998
It's an indescribable feeling.

42:23.082 --> 42:25.876
You have to experience it firsthand
to know how it feels.

42:25.960 --> 42:28.337
But you even ran away from home.

42:28.921 --> 42:30.631
Do you still love your family that much?

42:30.714 --> 42:33.092
Still, family is all I have.

42:34.593 --> 42:38.764
Don't jump from one office
to another like I did.

42:39.348 --> 42:41.141
Try to stay with your family.

42:41.225 --> 42:43.477
Living apart from your family
for a long time

42:44.645 --> 42:46.230
doesn't do you any good.

42:46.772 --> 42:48.732
You see… What?

42:50.317 --> 42:52.278
Stop by after you clock out.

42:52.361 --> 42:53.487
What's going on?

42:53.571 --> 42:54.947
Hey, my wife…

42:55.739 --> 42:57.741
- Okay.
- Hey.

42:57.825 --> 42:59.368
- Go in first.
- Okay.

42:59.451 --> 43:02.371
- I need to stop by my house.
- Sure. See you.

43:02.454 --> 43:04.290
- Okay. Bye.
- Bye.

43:05.165 --> 43:06.667
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

43:12.298 --> 43:13.132
Hello.

43:13.215 --> 43:15.426
Hello. What is it this time?

43:16.677 --> 43:19.096
- Please take this.
- What is this?

43:19.179 --> 43:20.347
It's kimchi.

43:20.931 --> 43:24.852
My mom wanted to thank you for
holding on to the side dishes last time.

43:24.935 --> 43:26.228
She didn't have to.

43:26.312 --> 43:29.023
Please. I'm sorry,

43:29.106 --> 43:31.775
but may I go inside and wash my hands?

43:31.859 --> 43:33.819
I think I spilled some on my way here.

43:34.612 --> 43:36.947
- My hands smell like kimchi.
- Gosh.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.157
Hold on.

43:38.240 --> 43:39.783
- Thank you.
- What? Wait.

43:40.451 --> 43:42.620
Excuse me? Ma'am?

43:53.172 --> 43:54.381
Doors opening.

44:01.472 --> 44:03.307
What are you doing there?

44:03.390 --> 44:04.892
What? Well…

44:05.392 --> 44:07.144
You see…

44:09.146 --> 44:10.105
Come inside.

44:10.189 --> 44:11.982
No, it's okay.

44:12.066 --> 44:14.276
By the way, take this.

44:14.777 --> 44:16.028
- Here.
- Okay.

44:16.111 --> 44:18.197
Take this inside.

44:19.073 --> 44:21.867
But you came all the way here. Come in.

44:21.950 --> 44:23.202
But I…

44:25.412 --> 44:26.872
Then I'll just stop by.

44:26.955 --> 44:28.415
Okay.

44:42.388 --> 44:44.264
Why are you back here again?

44:45.099 --> 44:46.892
Am I not allowed to?

44:46.975 --> 44:48.477
I brought some side dishes.

44:48.560 --> 44:49.812
Happy?

44:54.066 --> 44:57.194
Don't barge in like this
when I'm not living alone.

44:57.277 --> 44:59.571
All the more reason why
I should come more often.

44:59.655 --> 45:01.824
You're living with two grown men.

45:04.952 --> 45:06.370
Why would you be worried?

45:06.453 --> 45:08.539
Get married and have a daughter first.

45:08.622 --> 45:10.541
Then we'll talk.

45:11.333 --> 45:13.752
Anyway, you should leave soon.

45:13.836 --> 45:16.380
Senior Forecaster Um will arrive soon.
He'll be uncomfortable.

45:16.463 --> 45:19.425
I was going to leave even if
you begged me not to, so don't worry.

45:19.508 --> 45:21.510
- Good grief.
- Ma'am.

45:21.593 --> 45:23.470
Have some of this before you go.

45:24.221 --> 45:25.264
What?

45:25.347 --> 45:27.349
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

45:28.100 --> 45:31.603
But what's taking her so long?

45:32.271 --> 45:33.397
Who?

45:37.776 --> 45:38.819
Well…

45:40.404 --> 45:43.949
You see, I…

45:50.789 --> 45:51.748
Here.

45:52.666 --> 45:54.209
Thank you.

46:03.760 --> 46:06.013
You must be very well-versed.

46:06.096 --> 46:09.433
I'm just reading the bare minimum.

46:09.516 --> 46:10.726
So cocky.

46:10.809 --> 46:12.060
Sorry?

46:12.144 --> 46:14.104
Oh, I just said you were incredible.

46:14.688 --> 46:15.606
I see.

46:18.358 --> 46:22.154
Your mother didn't need to give me this.

46:22.738 --> 46:26.325
Our family's motto is to repay kindness.

46:26.408 --> 46:28.869
And who doesn't need side dishes?

46:28.952 --> 46:30.704
Don't you need to eat too?

46:30.787 --> 46:32.331
I cook single servings.

46:33.457 --> 46:35.083
You're the neat type.

46:35.667 --> 46:37.377
An only child? Or are you the eldest son?

46:37.461 --> 46:39.588
- I'm an only child.
- Where's your hometown?

46:39.671 --> 46:41.215
Suwon. Why do you ask?

46:41.298 --> 46:43.091
I just want to get to know

46:43.175 --> 46:44.676
my sister's colleague.

46:44.760 --> 46:47.137
I see. Well, anyway…

46:47.221 --> 46:49.723
Please tell your mother I said thank you.

46:49.806 --> 46:52.559
- But next time--
- Same team, same apartment, and neighbors.

46:53.435 --> 46:56.313
Don't you think
you two were destined to meet?

46:56.396 --> 47:00.234
Many KMA people live around here.

47:01.068 --> 47:04.780
I know six colleagues
who live in this same apartment.

47:05.364 --> 47:07.074
That's a lot.

47:24.383 --> 47:27.344
CITY CROCODILE
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

47:34.142 --> 47:35.227
You see…

47:36.144 --> 47:39.064
It may have lacked research,

47:39.147 --> 47:42.234
but the plot wasn't too bad.

47:46.446 --> 47:47.906
Which part did you like?

47:56.832 --> 47:57.958
What?

47:58.041 --> 48:00.085
You made her do what?

48:00.168 --> 48:01.795
Look. Hear me out first.

48:01.878 --> 48:03.672
- What's your problem?
- Goodness.

48:04.298 --> 48:05.841
Was I not clear enough?

48:05.924 --> 48:08.594
Assistant Director Shin is my subordinate.

48:08.677 --> 48:11.138
I'm upset, but what about him?

48:11.221 --> 48:12.764
What would he think of me?

48:14.141 --> 48:17.394
If you want someone to rely on,
you should find a man for yourself!

48:18.729 --> 48:21.481
How dare you say that?

48:21.565 --> 48:23.275
That's no way to talk to your mom.

48:23.358 --> 48:26.236
Do you know how it feels
to lose sleep worrying about your kid?

48:26.945 --> 48:28.363
I'm doing this for you.

48:28.447 --> 48:30.115
What a rude brat. What did you say?

48:30.198 --> 48:31.408
I should find a man?

48:32.784 --> 48:34.077
That's not right.

48:36.830 --> 48:39.583
See? Even he disagrees.

48:41.043 --> 48:42.419
No, ma'am.

48:42.502 --> 48:45.631
I disagree with you, not Director Jin.

48:46.923 --> 48:47.966
What?

48:48.050 --> 48:51.511
Rarely do people feel happy
when their parents force them to do things

48:52.012 --> 48:54.389
on the pretext of doing it for their kids.

48:55.724 --> 48:57.809
Hold on. Then tell me.

48:57.893 --> 49:01.521
Should I just sit back
and watch as she gets older?

49:02.147 --> 49:04.191
Should I let her
give up her opportunities,

49:04.274 --> 49:06.234
decent men, and her youth?

49:06.318 --> 49:07.944
Even if it's a great opportunity,

49:08.028 --> 49:10.072
wouldn't it be useless
if she doesn't want it?

49:10.822 --> 49:14.242
You don't know what you're talking about.

49:14.326 --> 49:16.870
- When it comes to marriage--
- I'm not getting married.

49:18.413 --> 49:19.581
What?

49:23.001 --> 49:25.045
I'm not getting married, Mom.

49:29.675 --> 49:33.053
Goodness. It's getting late.

49:33.136 --> 49:35.555
You should rest up.
We'll talk again tomorrow.

49:36.139 --> 49:37.140
I'm serious.

49:38.475 --> 49:40.519
I've made up my mind. I'm not going to.

49:42.312 --> 49:44.022
Hey, Ha-kyung.

49:45.232 --> 49:49.361
You didn't have to
say something so extreme.

49:49.444 --> 49:52.030
I get it. I was way out of line today.

49:52.114 --> 49:54.324
Let's just say
I crossed the line a little.

49:55.117 --> 49:56.326
I won't get married.

49:57.494 --> 50:00.747
I've decided I don't want to get married.

50:00.831 --> 50:03.667
So don't mention marriage, blind dates,

50:03.750 --> 50:05.210
or men to me ever again.

50:06.128 --> 50:06.962
Ha-kyung.

50:07.045 --> 50:09.381
I can't see you out today. Go home safely.

50:28.275 --> 50:31.194
That's why crocodiles' hind feet
have four toes.

50:32.112 --> 50:33.113
Gosh.

50:34.156 --> 50:36.241
You're a scientist.

50:36.742 --> 50:38.535
No, this is nothing impressive.

50:39.119 --> 50:40.829
Of course, it is.

50:40.912 --> 50:43.373
You know so much about animals.

50:45.459 --> 50:47.127
It's not that I'm a scientist.

50:47.210 --> 50:49.796
I just have a lot of interest in animals.

50:50.714 --> 50:51.798
I see.

50:53.300 --> 50:55.135
What about penguins?

50:55.218 --> 50:57.179
Do you know much about them?

50:57.929 --> 50:58.889
Penguins?

51:00.390 --> 51:03.059
Actually, I'm planning my next story,

51:03.143 --> 51:04.853
and the main character is a penguin.

51:06.229 --> 51:08.106
So I was wondering if you knew anything.

51:09.900 --> 51:13.361
Penguins are my favorite animal.

51:14.112 --> 51:15.572
No way. Are you serious?

51:15.655 --> 51:18.492
- Yes.
- That's great!

51:19.117 --> 51:20.744
Then can you help me?

51:20.827 --> 51:21.745
What?

51:23.455 --> 51:24.331
Please?

51:25.165 --> 51:27.125
Goodness. Well…

51:28.710 --> 51:30.212
You tell her.

51:30.879 --> 51:31.880
What do you mean?

51:32.380 --> 51:34.966
Tell Bo-mi yourself.

51:35.050 --> 51:36.885
Tell her what?

51:36.968 --> 51:40.222
Tell her not to visit the KMA next week.

51:40.305 --> 51:41.848
You're busy.

51:43.809 --> 51:46.812
It's fine. She won't take up my time.

51:47.813 --> 51:50.857
We've always offered
that field trip program.

51:51.775 --> 51:54.194
And it makes me happy to see her there.

51:55.153 --> 51:56.071
Not me.

51:57.572 --> 52:00.367
I don't want to see you and Bo-mi

52:00.951 --> 52:02.244
at the KMA together.

52:33.441 --> 52:34.901
Why are you following me?

52:35.402 --> 52:37.946
I'll help you get a cab. It's hot out.

52:39.322 --> 52:40.448
Goodness.

52:41.700 --> 52:42.909
Back in the day,

52:43.535 --> 52:46.788
it never got this sweltering.

52:47.831 --> 52:51.334
But the weather now is similar
to how people are these days.

52:51.418 --> 52:53.169
It's mercilessly hot.

52:54.546 --> 52:56.965
Despite that,
everyone works hard in this heat.

52:57.048 --> 52:58.258
They're all incredible.

52:58.967 --> 53:01.052
Incredible, my foot. They're merciless.

53:01.136 --> 53:04.806
But you need to be merciless and tough
to survive in this dog-eat-dog world.

53:06.558 --> 53:07.601
Was I that harsh?

53:07.684 --> 53:09.811
No, ma'am. That's not what I meant.

53:11.479 --> 53:12.647
Just forecast accurately.

53:12.731 --> 53:15.108
We're trying our best.

53:16.484 --> 53:17.903
Unbelievable.

53:20.030 --> 53:21.698
Oh, right. Ma'am.

53:21.781 --> 53:25.660
Don't worry too much about Director Jin.
She was probably in a fit of anger.

53:25.744 --> 53:29.205
The decision to never get married

53:29.289 --> 53:31.416
is never made overnight.

53:34.961 --> 53:37.756
No one knows her better than I do.

53:39.299 --> 53:42.385
She's not the type to say
such a thing in a fit of anger.

53:45.764 --> 53:48.183
Maybe I pushed her over the edge.

54:24.469 --> 54:26.262
She took a cab.

54:32.602 --> 54:34.479
She's a bit peculiar, isn't she?

54:38.441 --> 54:39.275
A bit.

54:41.277 --> 54:42.779
Actually, a lot.

54:44.572 --> 54:46.491
They're all like that
with their daughters.

54:47.075 --> 54:49.869
If you knew that,
why did you say that to her?

54:49.953 --> 54:51.162
Say what?

54:52.455 --> 54:53.665
About not getting married.

54:54.791 --> 54:57.961
I heard it's pretty shocking to hear
when you're on the receiving end.

54:58.044 --> 55:00.088
I know you didn't mean it,
but that was wrong.

55:00.797 --> 55:02.048
I did mean it.

55:04.801 --> 55:07.095
I'm seriously debating.

55:07.804 --> 55:11.433
I agree with you. Dating with marriage
in mind can feel suffocating.

55:11.516 --> 55:14.686
And I don't want us
to be a burden to each other.

55:24.154 --> 55:26.614
I'm tired. Let's go to bed.

56:35.517 --> 56:38.269
Due to the high temperature and humidity
of the North Pacific's anticyclone,

56:38.353 --> 56:40.647
the highest daytime temperature
will be 32°C.

56:40.730 --> 56:43.608
And the tropical nights will continue.

56:43.691 --> 56:46.861
Here's the issue.
Due to the ongoing tropical nights,

56:46.945 --> 56:48.822
people will become exhausted.

56:48.905 --> 56:51.866
This will lead to lack of focus
at work and more accidents.

56:51.950 --> 56:53.368
If you look at the chart…

56:57.330 --> 56:58.957
The Administrator wants to see you.

57:00.959 --> 57:01.960
Why?

57:02.669 --> 57:04.295
We're having a meeting. Tell me.

57:19.018 --> 57:20.228
Director Jin.

57:20.979 --> 57:22.397
Did you upload

57:22.480 --> 57:25.275
incorrect information
on the portal site yesterday?

57:30.071 --> 57:31.406
Yes, it was very brief.

57:31.906 --> 57:33.950
We corrected it right away.

57:40.582 --> 57:41.791
And you're telling me now?

57:43.126 --> 57:45.879
You should have reported it
to me right away!

57:47.547 --> 57:52.010
We're labeled as "erroneous" and "liars."
And now what? "Faulty"?

57:53.887 --> 57:55.263
What have you done?

57:55.763 --> 57:58.016
MUNMIN DAILY
INCORRECT INFORMATION ON PORTAL SITE

58:01.519 --> 58:02.854
Good grief.

58:04.314 --> 58:06.941
- Where is the Administrator?
- He's in his office.

58:07.692 --> 58:08.735
Goodness.

58:10.069 --> 58:11.112
Hello, sir.

58:12.071 --> 58:13.239
Yes, sir.

58:14.157 --> 58:15.325
May I look at that?

58:19.662 --> 58:21.748
MUNMIN DAILY
INCORRECT INFORMATION ON PORTAL SITE

58:23.333 --> 58:26.002
Damn it. When did they see this?

58:40.683 --> 58:42.936
Those reporters are all insane!

58:43.520 --> 58:45.647
Did they seriously write
an article about this?

58:46.231 --> 58:47.607
We're not machines.

58:47.690 --> 58:49.859
It's not like we always make mistakes.

58:52.737 --> 58:54.405
I mean, this was a first.

58:54.489 --> 58:56.282
How could they nitpick about this?

59:04.499 --> 59:06.876
But why is a society journalist here?

59:07.502 --> 59:09.212
And why is Reporter Chae with him?

59:14.717 --> 59:15.552
Come on.

59:16.135 --> 59:18.638
He didn't steal it.
I just chose not to write about it.

59:21.516 --> 59:22.642
I mean…

59:23.226 --> 59:25.436
If the media nitpicks
about such trivial issues,

59:25.520 --> 59:27.564
how will these people work?

59:28.147 --> 59:29.691
Yes. Of course.

59:33.236 --> 59:34.737
Thank you for understanding.

59:35.446 --> 59:36.406
Okay.

59:37.865 --> 59:39.033
Goodbye.

59:49.752 --> 59:51.170
We need to talk.

01:00:03.933 --> 01:00:05.018
What's this about?

01:00:06.144 --> 01:00:08.479
The incorrect information
on the portal site.

01:00:08.563 --> 01:00:10.023
You told him, didn't you?

01:00:10.815 --> 01:00:11.899
It wasn't me.

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:13.318
I already saw everything.

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:16.362
I saw you chatting
with that guy, Butcher Heo.

01:00:16.446 --> 01:00:17.655
It wasn't me.

01:00:17.739 --> 01:00:19.198
What's wrong with you?

01:00:20.408 --> 01:00:21.951
You've been here for a while,

01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:23.620
so you know how things are.

01:00:23.703 --> 01:00:25.204
Couldn't you have turned a blind eye?

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:26.331
How about you guys?

01:00:26.414 --> 01:00:28.041
Don't you make typos?

01:00:30.752 --> 01:00:32.045
You're not interested

01:00:33.087 --> 01:00:35.256
in hearing me out, are you?

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:36.507
Why bother

01:00:37.008 --> 01:00:38.843
when you're always denying everything?

01:00:42.347 --> 01:00:44.057
How did you even marry me?

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:46.059
What?

01:00:46.142 --> 01:00:48.102
Why did you even marry me

01:00:48.186 --> 01:00:51.189
if you won't believe me
or even hear me out?

01:00:51.272 --> 01:00:54.484
Yu-jin, why are you suddenly
dragging us into this?

01:00:54.567 --> 01:00:56.194
I was talking about the article.

01:00:56.277 --> 01:00:58.946
And I'm talking
about the trust between us.

01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:02.367
Seeing how much you're doubting me,

01:01:02.450 --> 01:01:04.285
I should be worried

01:01:04.369 --> 01:01:07.288
not just as a journalist
but also as your wife.

01:01:09.082 --> 01:01:10.208
Am I wrong?

01:01:15.797 --> 01:01:16.964
Director Jin.

01:01:17.799 --> 01:01:19.926
Why can't you manage your team properly?

01:01:20.927 --> 01:01:21.928
I'm sorry, sir.

01:01:22.011 --> 01:01:25.181
Why does this keep happening? Tell me.

01:01:25.264 --> 01:01:27.433
Your team is causing headaches
every single day.

01:01:28.434 --> 01:01:31.771
Do you think you'll be able to hold out

01:01:31.854 --> 01:01:33.773
during the disaster prevention period?

01:01:33.856 --> 01:01:34.691
Do you?

01:01:35.733 --> 01:01:37.360
If you can't, let me know.

01:01:37.443 --> 01:01:39.987
Then I'll send you more people
or come up with something.

01:01:40.071 --> 01:01:41.823
I'll work harder.

01:01:41.906 --> 01:01:44.200
Teamwork is crucial

01:01:44.283 --> 01:01:45.618
once the typhoon hits.

01:01:47.245 --> 01:01:48.579
Keep that in mind.

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:51.290
Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:52.667
Go on.

01:01:53.376 --> 01:01:55.211
Who will be going to Jeju Island?

01:01:55.837 --> 01:01:56.796
Sorry?

01:01:56.879 --> 01:01:59.799
The typhoon is slowly advancing.

01:01:59.882 --> 01:02:01.843
Someone needs to go to the typhoon center.

01:02:01.926 --> 01:02:04.887
- Have you not chosen someone yet?
- Not yet, sir.

01:02:19.068 --> 01:02:19.986
Oh, no.

01:02:25.074 --> 01:02:26.075
I'm sorry,

01:02:27.368 --> 01:02:29.245
but I need to go first.

01:02:30.371 --> 01:02:33.332
I need to pick up my kids.

01:02:34.375 --> 01:02:36.627
Sure. Go on. It's okay.

01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:37.962
Okay. Soo-jin.

01:02:38.045 --> 01:02:40.006
Could you update

01:02:40.089 --> 01:02:42.175
Assistant Director Cho for me?

01:02:42.258 --> 01:02:44.218
I'll deliver important details via phone.

01:02:44.302 --> 01:02:46.012
Okay. I'll do that.

01:02:46.888 --> 01:02:48.264
Thank you.

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:59.025
I can't believe she left

01:02:59.734 --> 01:03:01.819
when Director Jin is getting an earful.

01:03:02.403 --> 01:03:04.280
She was the one who made the mistake,

01:03:04.363 --> 01:03:06.866
but Director Jin chose not to report it.

01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:13.998
Where's Assistant Director Oh?

01:03:15.124 --> 01:03:16.375
She just left.

01:03:17.543 --> 01:03:20.213
She had to pick up her kids,
so I told her to go first.

01:03:22.048 --> 01:03:24.008
It's already time.

01:03:24.592 --> 01:03:26.093
You should all go home.

01:03:26.177 --> 01:03:27.303
- Okay.
- Okay.

01:03:47.490 --> 01:03:49.534
Pick someone and tell them right away.

01:03:49.617 --> 01:03:52.078
They will have to be there
for at least two months.

01:04:47.174 --> 01:04:48.342
Is something wrong?

01:04:49.385 --> 01:04:50.386
What?

01:04:50.970 --> 01:04:52.096
No. Why?

01:04:52.179 --> 01:04:54.348
There seems to be something
on your mind ever since you talked

01:04:54.432 --> 01:04:55.725
to the Director General.

01:04:56.642 --> 01:04:58.895
Oh, it's because of the typhoon center.

01:05:00.646 --> 01:05:02.607
Soon, it'll be typhoon season.

01:05:02.690 --> 01:05:05.776
Someone from our team
needs to go to Jeju Island.

01:05:05.860 --> 01:05:07.236
I see.

01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:15.745
Can you go?

01:05:20.124 --> 01:05:21.542
You should go, Forecaster Lee.

01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.228
Let's spend some time apart.

01:05:44.523 --> 01:05:46.442
What are you talking about?

01:05:49.236 --> 01:05:50.613
I want some time apart.

01:05:52.406 --> 01:05:54.408
I think that's best for both of us.

01:05:55.660 --> 01:05:56.577
Yu-jin.

01:05:56.661 --> 01:05:59.038
We need some time to think.

01:05:59.121 --> 01:06:01.207
Let's evaluate our relationship.

01:06:03.167 --> 01:06:05.544
Be honest. You need some time alone too.

01:06:15.972 --> 01:06:17.264
Do you mean that?

01:06:18.432 --> 01:06:20.685
I'm never half-hearted
when it comes to work.

01:06:26.482 --> 01:06:27.858
That means

01:06:28.776 --> 01:06:30.945
you've already made up your mind.

01:06:32.863 --> 01:06:35.116
Yes. If it's all right with you.

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:48.963
Is this because

01:06:49.672 --> 01:06:51.590
of what happened today?

01:06:52.258 --> 01:06:55.094
Anyone would have
misunderstood that situation.

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.887
You would have been mad if you were me.

01:06:56.971 --> 01:06:58.222
No.

01:06:58.305 --> 01:07:00.641
I would have heard
your side of the story first.

01:07:03.644 --> 01:07:04.895
Okay. So?

01:07:05.563 --> 01:07:07.398
You're really going to leave?

01:07:07.481 --> 01:07:09.191
I want to breathe.

01:07:09.275 --> 01:07:11.485
Whenever I see you frown at home,

01:07:11.569 --> 01:07:13.279
I wonder if it's because of me again.

01:07:13.362 --> 01:07:14.989
Do you know how suffocating it is?

01:07:15.823 --> 01:07:17.742
I never suffocated you.

01:07:17.825 --> 01:07:20.786
You're doing it right now.
You can't understand me.

01:07:22.204 --> 01:07:25.374
Do you know how frustrating
and suffocating that is?

01:07:26.292 --> 01:07:28.419
Can you say that you understand me?

01:07:29.962 --> 01:07:33.466
I abandoned a relationship of ten years
because I wanted to marry you.

01:07:33.549 --> 01:07:36.010
Can you please stop telling me
about how you left her?

01:07:37.595 --> 01:07:39.513
Can you please stop?

01:07:39.597 --> 01:07:42.099
I only said that
because you didn't think I loved you.

01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:45.102
That's why you won't register our marriage
and are worried about the future.

01:07:45.186 --> 01:07:46.520
Exactly!

01:07:47.938 --> 01:07:51.108
So can we please have
some alone time and think about this?

01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:55.738
Let's figure out
what's best for both of us.

01:08:07.958 --> 01:08:11.128
On such nights, we become lost in thought.

01:08:18.094 --> 01:08:20.179
Ha-kyung doesn't sincerely date anyone

01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:22.056
if they're not a marriage prospect.

01:08:22.139 --> 01:08:23.891
You knew that, right?

01:08:24.475 --> 01:08:26.185
If it's not marriage,

01:08:26.268 --> 01:08:28.729
what could be

01:08:29.438 --> 01:08:30.815
awaiting us at the end?

01:08:37.822 --> 01:08:41.867
When that happens,
we end up having complicated feelings

01:08:42.701 --> 01:08:44.078
and that leads

01:08:45.204 --> 01:08:46.831
to more thoughts.

01:08:48.124 --> 01:08:49.208
And eventually,

01:08:50.709 --> 01:08:52.545
we become even more lost in thought.

01:09:28.998 --> 01:09:33.627
In this way,
our sleepless tropical night wore on.

01:10:03.824 --> 01:10:05.201
If you leave like this,

01:10:05.284 --> 01:10:06.702
it's really over between us.

01:10:06.785 --> 01:10:08.412
Have you thought about that?

01:10:08.495 --> 01:10:09.622
Who's going to the typhoon center?

01:10:09.705 --> 01:10:10.664
I'm going.

01:10:10.748 --> 01:10:12.291
I know you want to draw clear lines

01:10:12.374 --> 01:10:14.126
between the KMA, me, work, and dating.

01:10:14.210 --> 01:10:17.504
You compare me to him every time,
and it really bothers me.

01:10:17.588 --> 01:10:20.007
I want things to work out between us.

01:10:20.090 --> 01:10:23.177
Why do you keep confusing me?

01:10:25.221 --> 01:10:27.848
Help! A student is down on the floor!

01:10:28.474 --> 01:10:29.642
What? An accident?

01:10:30.517 --> 01:10:31.852
Lee Si-woo.

01:10:31.936 --> 01:10:33.437
He works at the KMA.

01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:39.151
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
